Work order text TK-20261120-8382 (submitted on 2026-10-01, source: inspection)
Product link: SO-20260925-132407, category listed under “Household small appliances”; what is actually sold is soft contact lenses (contact lenses), and the detail page states “daily disposable, 30-piece pack, can be worn continuously for 12 hours.”
Verification process:
1. This category belongs to Class III medical devices and must have both a Medical Device Business License and a product registration certificate number;
2. The merchant qualification field is empty; only one business license was uploaded, and its business scope does not include medical device sales;
3. The backend sent three requests to submit the missing documents (2026-11-01, 2026-11-12, 2026-10-08); the merchant did not submit them on any occasion and replied “other stores sell it this way too”;
4. The page does not mark any contraindications or wearing warnings.
Conclusion and recommendation: It is a prohibited sale or missing qualifications; delist the product immediately, and record one serious violation against the store.
One additional note: what a logistics dispatcher asked about yesterday was the arrival time for B-39406; it has nothing to do with this work order, so do not mix up the orders.

